    ; instance, runs to U+FFFD), and without one the built-in REFERENCE
    ; declaration applies: DESCSET leaves the C0 controls other than
    ; TAB/RS/RE (9/10/13) UNUSED, then DEL (127) and the whole C1 range
    ; 128..159 (the ECMA-94 right part starts at 160), so those are the
    ; non-SGML chars. Measured against onsgmls: bytes 0x82 and 0x9F in an
    ; 8-bit-read document report nonSgmlCharacter, 0xA0..0xFF do not.
    ;
