    ;     the fixed internal charset is the system charset, identity over
    ;     0..INTERNAL_CHAR_MAX (see CharsetDecl.scaly) — in range translates
    ;     the char, beyond it reports numericCharRefNoInternal (E1, at the
    ;     REFC). The reference's numericCharRefBadInternal arm (ambiguous /
    ;     over-charMax internal mapping) is unreachable with an identity map.
